/*
Detection Rule: Azure Blob Storage Anomalous Download Activity
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1530 - Data from Cloud Storage
Severity: High
Description: Detects anomalous bulk read activity against Azure Blob Storage
containers including high-volume GetBlob operations, access via AzCopy or
command-line tooling, SAS token authenticated bulk reads, and anonymous
access to storage containers. Blob storage frequently contains sensitive
business data, application backups, and credentials — making it a high-value
exfiltration target when Azure credentials are compromised.
*/

index=azure_storage sourcetype="azure:storage:blob"
    operationName IN ("GetBlob", "GetBlobProperties", "ListBlobs", "GetContainerProperties")
    statusCode=200

| eval actor=coalesce(properties.callerIpAddress, identity.requester.objectId)
| eval account_name=resourceId
| eval container_name=properties.containerName
| eval blob_name=properties.blobName
| eval bytes_read=coalesce(properties.contentLengthHeader, 0)
| eval auth_type=properties.authenticationType
| eval user_agent=properties.userAgentHeader

/* Classify the requesting client tool type */
| eval requester_type=case(
    match(user_agent, "azcopy|AzCopy"),                    "AzCopy",
    match(user_agent, "python-azure|azure-storage-python"), "Python SDK",
    match(user_agent, "curl|wget"),                         "Command Line",
    match(auth_type, "Anonymous"),                          "Anonymous",
    match(auth_type, "SAS"),                                "SAS Token",
    1==1,                                                   "Azure SDK")

/* Aggregate per storage account per 15-minute window */
| bin _time span=15m
| stats
    count                       AS blob_reads,
    dc(container_name)          AS distinct_containers,
    dc(blob_name)               AS distinct_blobs,
    sum(bytes_read)             AS total_bytes,
    values(container_name)      AS containers_accessed,
    values(requester_type)      AS requester_types,
    values(user_agent)          AS agents,
    values(auth_type)           AS auth_methods,
    values(actor)               AS actor_ips,
    min(_time)                  AS first_seen,
    max(_time)                  AS last_seen
    by account_name, _time

| eval total_mb=round(total_bytes / 1048576, 2)

| where blob_reads > 200
    OR distinct_containers > 5
    OR total_mb > 500
    OR match(requester_types, "Anonymous|Command Line")

/* Score based on volume, tool type, and auth method */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(match(auth_methods,"Anonymous") AND total_mb > 100,     risk_score+65, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(requester_types,"AzCopy") AND total_mb > 500,     risk_score+55, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(requester_types,"Command Line") AND blob_reads>100, risk_score+50, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(blob_reads > 1000 AND distinct_containers > 5,          risk_score+45, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(auth_methods,"Anonymous"),                        risk_score+30, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(total_mb > 500,                                         risk_score+20, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(blob_reads > 200,                                       risk_score+10, risk_score)

| eval alert_title="Azure Blob Storage Exfiltration Suspected: " . account_name
| table _time, alert_title, account_name, blob_reads, distinct_containers,
        distinct_blobs, total_mb, containers_accessed,
        requester_types, auth_methods, actor_ips,
        risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- blob_reads threshold: Establish baseline per storage account over 30 days;
  set threshold at mean + 2 standard deviations per account
- total_mb threshold: Adjust based on largest legitimate ETL workload in environment
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(account_name, "backupsa|datasync|etlpipeline|azbackup")
  | where NOT match(requester_types, "Azure SDK")
  | where account_name!="<known-media-streaming-storage-account>"

FALSE POSITIVES:
- Azure Data Factory or Synapse Analytics pipelines performing bulk reads for ETL
- AzCopy used by approved backup or data migration projects
- Media streaming services reading large blob assets at high volume
- Azure Backup or Azure Site Recovery performing scheduled backup reads

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Identify the requesting entity — service principal object ID, user, or anonymous
2. Determine if this is a known scheduled data pipeline or an ad-hoc request
3. Assess the data classification of the containers accessed
4. Rotate SAS tokens if SAS authentication was involved
5. Apply network ACL to restrict storage account access to approved VNet subnets
6. If anonymous access confirmed: disable public blob access on the storage account immediately

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- All blobs accessed by actor: index=azure_storage sourcetype="azure:storage:blob"
  properties.callerIpAddress=<actor_ip> earliest=<first_seen> latest=<last_seen>
  | stats count by properties.containerName, properties.blobName
- Anonymous access check: index=azure_storage sourcetype="azure:storage:blob"
  properties.authenticationType="Anonymous" account_name=<account_name>
  | table _time, properties.containerName, properties.blobName, properties.callerIpAddress
- Current public access status: index=azure_activity
  operationName="Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/read"
  resourceId=<account_name> | table _time, properties.responseBody

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- Azure Storage Diagnostic Logs (enabled per-storage-account under Diagnostic Settings)
- Must stream StorageRead logs via Event Hub or Azure Monitor to Splunk
- This logging is NOT enabled by default on storage accounts

HIGH-RISK INDICATORS:
- auth_type is Anonymous (no credentials required — data is publicly readable)
- AzCopy tool used with high volume (purpose-built for bulk transfer)
- Source IP resolves to a residential ISP or known VPN provider
- Access patterns follow enumerate-then-download: ListBlobs → GetBlob sequence

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Enforce private endpoints for all storage accounts containing sensitive data
- Apply Azure Policy to deny public blob access at the subscription level
- Disable shared key access and require Azure AD authentication for all storage
- Enable Microsoft Defender for Storage for real-time anomaly alerting

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1619 - Cloud Storage Object Discovery
- T1537 - Transfer Data to Cloud Account
- T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
